	"description": [
		"This course familiarizes the student with the major management functions of planning, organizing, leading, and controlling. The study of management theory is linked with application exercises. Students begin to develop the management skills necessary in any organization, whether it be a for-profit or not-for-profit venture, a small business, or a large corporation. Offered each semester. Prerequisite: sophomore standing or above, or permission of instructor."
